Cell["\<\
We make some 3 axis acceleration measurements using the TinkerForge \
Accelerometer Bricklet  or the TinkerForge IMU Brick (or Bricklet) connected \
to the Master Brick using the Logger functionality in the Brick Viewer as \
shown in class.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.947791309379293*^9, 3.947791389990486*^9}, {
  3.9478489536465273`*^9, 3.947849011733878*^9}, {3.947849108707878*^9, 
  3.947849160961851*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"62c8f80d-a9ca-4148-b283-\
79443bd1de10"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Import .CSV file from TinkerForge Brick Viewer Logger", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.947789278471216*^9, 
  3.94778930314192*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c12aeab2-bfa1-4a07-acbf-\
31a2d8f6d055"],

Cell["\<\
When you set up the Logger in the Brick Viewer save the filename. Replace the \
following with your file name:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.947789313780582*^9, 3.947789370873364*^9}, {
  3.947844841282052*^9, 
  3.9478448616664963`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d923f6fa-e656-496a-ab2d-\
f0e1a9671877"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"file", "=", "\"\<\\Users\\ariel\\Downloads\\IMU.csv\>\""}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.947789178988305*^9, 3.947789188574853*^9}, 
   3.9477893773867617`*^9, {3.9477917135248337`*^9, 3.947791718349369*^9}, {
   3.979298919633511*^9, 3.9792989237339993`*^9}, {3.979298965688377*^9, 
   3.979298970292238*^9}, {3.9792993791322117`*^9, 3.979299384388215*^9}, {
   3.9793052107324905`*^9, 3.9793052110902424`*^9}, {3.9793052543256435`*^9, 
   3.979305284633524*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[33]:=",ExpressionUUID->"92aeefaf-cf8f-42ae-b508-f944e173a65a"],

Cell["\<\
Note that you will need to change the file name in the Logger for each \
repeated measurement you make (it does not seem to overwrite existing files). \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.947792045138053*^9, 
  3.947792135505239*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"40fe134c-7922-4762-9547-\
394c17819a4c"],

Cell["\<\
Now we can import the CSV data using  the function Import[]. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.947789388378467*^9, 3.947789487234928*^9}, {
  3.94779216347438*^9, 
  3.947792170513618*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"18fe4ce5-0215-448b-8aca-\
72a14b7a5033"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Import", "[", "file", "]"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9477921861292953`*^9, 3.9477922148576717`*^9}, {
   3.947792279133019*^9, 3.947792326323737*^9}, 3.94784452894932*^9, {
   3.979305180790682*^9, 3.979305200335123*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[34]:=",ExpressionUUID->"57f7dee5-209b-455d-bfa1-b0f6c5e5e124"],

Cell["\<\
You can suppress the output by including a ; at the end of the line.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9477922275742807`*^9, 
  3.947792273714305*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"53863743-56fa-456b-a7c9-\
56a23ce3005a"],

Cell["\<\
Note that TinkerForge stores the logged data using \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote];\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] as delimiters. We want them to be converted to \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote],\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. The following achieves what \
we want:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.947789388378467*^9, 3.947789487234928*^9}, 
   3.94779216347438*^9},ExpressionUUID->"b3d10e6e-e634-43bf-8c9f-\
a3a9240cec52"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"data", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Import", "[", 
    RowBox[{"file", ",", "\"\<Table\>\"", ",", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<FieldSeparators\>\"", "->", "\"\<;\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.947789170589403*^9, 3.947789170591805*^9}, {
   3.947789201711977*^9, 3.947789213620782*^9}, 3.979299003598448*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[35]:=",ExpressionUUID->"38f78535-5fb6-4e11-8e0a-d2339b3cf8c8"],

Cell["\<\
We can access the first row (the header information for the columns) using\
\>", "Text",
